      "writtenOn": "2026-11-18T08:03:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Comment says local credentials are only allowed with a localhost address, but server_address is not validated before CreateChannel(... LocalCredentials ...).\n\nIf a caller passes a non-loopback host while Grpc_Credentials\u003dlocal, this fails late or behaves unexpectedly. It would be better to validate the address (or assert loopback) before creating the channel.",
      "revId": "9ece5cc53dfb24b69090b2303f0659fe5a1ce345",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0683cd03_09b15341",
        "filename": "src/grpc_server/nfsServiceClient.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039498
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T14:54:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With local credentials, gRPC already rejects non-loopback connections during the handshake, so the first RPC fails right away. The address string can also use a hostname like localhost:50051 that gRPC resolves first, so I updated the comment instead.",
      "parentUuid": "017189d6_43f8062f",
      "revId": "9ece5cc53dfb24b69090b2303f0659fe5a1ce345",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
